message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Most lead-tainted spices are too dilute for a bulk Raman screen"
abstract: "Across FDA recalls, New York City lab tests and King County lab tests, almost no lead-contaminated spice reaches the detection limit of bench Raman on powder. A screen would need to be 10 to 20 times more sensitive to catch 9 in 10 of New York's high-lead samples. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
